Do not match a signal name against an empty slot of the signal table.
get_signum() strips an optional SIG prefix and compares the rest with
every entry of signals[], including those left empty for numbers the
platform does not define. An empty name, or SIG alone, so matched the
first such gap. On Windows "kill -s '' PID" and "kill -SIG PID" sent
signal 5 and failed with "Invalid argument", "kill -l SIG" printed 5,
and the shell's "trap CMD ''" succeeded. Skip empty entries, so these
names are rejected as unknown signals.

---
 libbb/u_signal_names.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/libbb/u_signal_names.c
+++ b/libbb/u_signal_names.c
@@ -172,7 +172,7 @@
 	if (strncasecmp(name, "SIG", 3) == 0)
 		name += 3;
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(signals); i++)
-		if (strcasecmp(name, signals[i]) == 0)
+		if (signals[i][0] && strcasecmp(name, signals[i]) == 0)
 			return i;
 
 #if ENABLE_DESKTOP
